-- $N$: Total number of geometric objects (primitives).
-- $n$: Target average number of objects per grid cell.
-- $MaxResolution$: User-specified maximum resolution along each axis.
-- $xSize, ySize, zSize$: Dimensions of the axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) containing all objects.
-- For each object: its AABB defined by $(x_{min}, y_{min}, z_{min})$ and $(x_{max}, y_{max}, z_{max})$.
