 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Resolution calculation is $O(1)$. Partitioning is $O(N \cdot k)$, where $N$ is the number of objects and $k$ is the average number of cells an object intersects. In the worst case (large objects), $k$ can be proportional to the grid volume.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(xResolution \times yResolution \times zResolution + N_{total\_references})$, where $N_{total\_references}$ is the total number of object-cell associations. Memory overhead increases with higher resolution [S1, unofficial].
