 - **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-- **Scaling:** Higher grid resolution reduces object partition size, leading to faster ray-object intersection tests. However, it increases memory overhead and the number of cells to traverse along a ray, which can counterbalance the speed-up [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Simple to implement; robust; provides a good baseline for acceleration structures.
-- **Limitations:** Inefficient for scenes with highly non-uniform object distribution; high memory usage for high resolutions; duplicate storage of objects in multiple cells.
-- **When to use:** Scenes with relatively uniform object distribution; when simplicity is prioritized over optimal performance.
-- **When not to use:** Scenes with large variations in object density; memory-constrained environments.
